  "title": "Dataform Workspaces Get Async Creation, `parent` Now Required",
  "summary": "Dataform introduces `createLongRunning` for asynchronous Workspace creation. This new method requires the `parent` parameter, which is a breaking change if you were previously omitting it in early integrations.",
  "details": "Developers can now asynchronously create Dataform Workspaces using the new `projects.locations.repositories.workspaces.createLongRunning` method. This method returns a long-running `Operation` for tracking the creation process. The `parent` parameter, specifying the repository path, and `workspaceId` are both required for this new method. \n\n**Breaking Change:** The `parent` parameter for `projects.locations.repositories.workspaces.createLongRunning` is now strictly required. If you were using an earlier version of this API where `parent` was optional for this method, your calls will now fail until you provide this parameter.",
